# Guarded production-only D1 migration execution instructions.
# This trigger is the sole path allowlisted by .github/workflows/d1-apply-0007.yml.
# The workflow uses its exact GITHUB_SHA, waits for /health to report that SHA,
# then selects the latest COMPLETED post-deploy growth cycle dynamically.

Apply only migrations/0007_demand_query_indexes.sql to the exact production database atlas_db (UUID a5a75faa-e800-4112-b67a-3c53d7b0d8d4) using wrangler d1 execute --remote --file after the allowlisted preflight succeeds. Require a current post-deploy COMPLETED growth cycle, exactly four matching source rows, corresponding demand_source_health updates, and AgentJob last_attempt_at younger than 30 minutes at preflight. Retain all other checks: demand_signals has 10 columns and 23 rows, signal_key NULL count = 0, duplicate groups = 0, all six exact indexes absent with no equivalent indexes, and a fresh same-run Time Travel bookmark younger than two hours captured once and rechecked immediately before execution. Postflight verifies all six exact index definitions and column order, idx_demand_signal_key unique, unchanged row counts for every table, and /health healthy at the same GITHUB_SHA. Do not run migrations apply, do not touch d1_migrations, and do not write any other SQL. On any preflight or postflight failure, stop and retain the state; no automatic DROP, delete, or restore. No Time Travel restore is authorized.


Approved execution trigger for the post-PR-190 0007 retry: run only through the allowlisted d1-apply-0007 workflow. It must use this exact main GITHUB_SHA, wait until production /health matches it, pass the full read-only preflight, capture and recheck one fresh same-run bookmark, and execute only migrations/0007_demand_query_indexes.sql with the approved postflight. No migrations apply, no d1_migrations changes, no direct D1 write, and no restore.
